<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giuseppe Verdi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1901</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Verdi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giuseppe Verdi was an Italian opera composer, born at Le Roncole near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/busseto">Busseto</a> in the Duchy of Parma. His operas, among them Nabucco, Rigoletto, La traviata, Il trovatore, Aida, Otello and Falstaff, made him the dominant figure of nineteenth-century Italian opera. Works such as I vespri siciliani and his public support for unification made him a symbol of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-unification">Risorgimento</a>, and he sat in the first Italian parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi.jpg" alt="Giuseppe Verdi" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ferdinand Mulnier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giuseppe_Verdi_by_Ferdinand_Mulnier_BW.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
